      "content": "I understand the concern for consistency, but standardizing the output may also result in a one-size-fits-all approach that neglects the unique needs and learning styles of individual students. By removing personality-driven feedback and empathetic responses, students may feel less invested in their learning, potentially leading to decreased engagement and motivation. Furthermore, standardizing the delivery of the curriculum may overlook opportunities for teachers to tailor the experience to their students' specific strengths and challenges. Would exploring alternative solutions, such as refining and standardizing the algorithm behind personalization, be worth investigating?",
      "source": "target",
